.TH KINTSUGI-REVIEW 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-review \- read-only code review of a diff
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi review
.RI [ ref ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-ship\-check ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the change, ask the gate model what is wrong with it, and print findings by
severity with a ship/no-ship verdict.
.PP
With no \fIref\fR the working tree is judged; with one, the diff against that ref
is (a branch name or a commit both work).
.PP
The reviewer is read-only by construction: it is handed a diff, it returns
findings, and it holds no tool access. Nothing here writes, stages or commits.
.PP
Findings are graded P0-P3. A P0 or P1 drives a no-ship verdict:
.IP \fBP0\fR
security vulnerabilities, data loss, crashes, correctness bugs
.IP \fBP1\fR
performance issues, resource leaks, race conditions
.IP \fBP2\fR
code quality, maintainability, missing error handling
.IP \fBP3\fR
style, naming, documentation
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-\-json\fR
Print the typed review as JSON.
.IP \fB\-\-ship\-check\fR
Exit non-zero when the verdict is no-ship, for use in a script.
.SH EXAMPLES
Review the working tree:
.PP
  $ kintsugi review
.PP
Review a branch:
.PP
  $ kintsugi review main
.PP
Fail a script on a no-ship verdict:
.PP
  $ kintsugi review --ship-check
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-gate (1),
.BR kintsugi-commit (1)
